1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,821
In this lesson, a BC topic, we'll find
slopes on parametric curves.

2
00:00:05,967 --> 00:00:14,119
If x and y both depend on t, the chain
rule gives d y d x equals d y d t over d x

3
00:00:14,119 --> 00:00:14,521
d t.

4
00:00:14,971 --> 00:00:18,043
Divide the vertical rate by the horizontal
rate.

5
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:26,483
For x equals t squared and y equals t
cubed minus three t: d x d t is two t, d y

6
00:00:26,483 --> 00:00:29,684
d t is three t squared minus three.

7
00:00:30,134 --> 00:00:34,977
So d y d x equals three t squared minus
three, over two t.

8
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:43,716
Horizontal tangents occur where d y d t is
zero and d x d t isn't: t equals plus or

9
00:00:43,716 --> 00:00:44,633
minus one.

10
00:00:45,083 --> 00:00:52,102
Vertical tangents occur where d x d t is
zero and d y d t isn't: t equals zero.

11
00:00:53,233 --> 00:01:00,361
The second derivative is the derivative of
d y d x with respect to t, divided by d x

12
00:01:00,361 --> 00:01:00,700
d t.

13
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:04,393
It's not just d squared y over d t
squared.

14
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:11,653
Find the tangent line at t equals two. The
point is four, two, and the slope is nine

15
00:01:11,653 --> 00:01:12,381
over four.

16
00:01:12,831 --> 00:01:16,799
y minus two equals nine fourths times x
minus four.

17
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:23,928
Your turn. Find d y d x for x equals
cosine t, y equals sine t.

18
00:01:24,378 --> 00:01:25,914
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:26,364 --> 00:01:31,185
Cosine t over negative sine t, which is
negative cotangent t.

20
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:37,496
In this lesson, a BC topic, we'll measure
distance along parametric paths.

21
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:44,628
The arc length from t equals a to b is the
integral of the square root of x prime

22
00:01:44,628 --> 00:01:47,145
squared plus y prime squared, d t.

23
00:01:47,595 --> 00:01:50,347
It adds tiny hypotenuses along the path.

24
00:01:51,466 --> 00:01:56,842
For x equals t squared, y equals two
thirds t cubed, from zero to one:

25
00:01:57,292 --> 00:02:03,034
x prime is two t, y prime is two t
squared. The integrand is two t times the

26
00:02:03,034 --> 00:02:09,077
square root of one plus t squared, which
integrates to two thirds times two root

27
00:02:09,077 --> 00:02:10,135
two minus one.

28
00:02:11,266 --> 00:02:16,294
If the curve is a particle's path, the
speed is the square root of x prime

29
00:02:16,294 --> 00:02:18,264
squared plus y prime squared.

30
00:02:18,714 --> 00:02:21,722
Speed is the integrand of the arc length
formula.

31
00:02:22,866 --> 00:02:28,962
For x equals three cosine t, y equals
three sine t, the speed is three at all

32
00:02:28,962 --> 00:02:29,437
times.

33
00:02:29,887 --> 00:02:34,111
From zero to two pi, the distance is six
pi, the circumference.

34
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:38,284
Total distance traveled is the integral of
speed.

35
00:02:38,734 --> 00:02:41,912
It's always positive, even if the path
doubles back.

36
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:49,412
Your turn. Find the speed at t equals one
for x equals t squared, y equals four t.

37
00:02:49,862 --> 00:02:51,398
Pause the video and try it.

38
00:02:51,848 --> 00:02:57,518
x prime is two, y prime is four, so the
speed is the square root of twenty, about

39
00:02:57,518 --> 00:02:59,058
four point four seven.

40
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:05,277
In this lesson, a BC topic, we'll describe
motion in the plane with vectors.

41
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:12,696
A vector-valued function r of t equals x
of t, y of t gives a position vector at

42
00:03:12,696 --> 00:03:13,483
each time.

43
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:16,066
Its tip traces the particle's path.

44
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:23,870
Differentiate componentwise. Velocity is x
prime, y prime, and acceleration is x

45
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:26,288
double prime, y double prime.

46
00:03:26,738 --> 00:03:29,362
The velocity vector is tangent to the
path.

47
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:33,487
Speed is the magnitude of the velocity
vector.

48
00:03:33,937 --> 00:03:36,241
Direction comes from the vector itself.

49
00:03:37,367 --> 00:03:44,328
r of t equals t squared, e to the t. Then
v equals two t, e to the t, and a equals

50
00:03:44,328 --> 00:03:45,687
two, e to the t.

51
00:03:46,137 --> 00:03:51,747
At t equals zero, the velocity is zero,
one: moving straight up with speed one.

52
00:03:52,867 --> 00:03:59,224
Integrate componentwise to go back. If a
equals zero, negative thirty two, v of

53
00:03:59,224 --> 00:04:03,811
zero equals ten, twenty, and r of zero
equals zero, zero:

54
00:04:04,261 --> 00:04:11,115
v equals ten, twenty minus thirty two t,
and r equals ten t, twenty t minus sixteen

55
00:04:11,115 --> 00:04:11,941
t squared.

56
00:04:13,067 --> 00:04:19,829
Your turn. Find the velocity of r of t
equals sine t, cosine t at t equals zero.

57
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:21,815
Pause the video and try it.

58
00:04:22,265 --> 00:04:28,388
v equals cosine t, negative sine t, which
is one, zero at t equals zero.

59
00:04:29,533 --> 00:04:33,842
In this lesson, a BC topic, we'll find
slopes of polar curves.

60
00:04:34,966 --> 00:04:42,281
A polar curve r equals f of theta is a
parametric curve: x equals r cosine theta,

61
00:04:42,281 --> 00:04:44,268
y equals r sine theta.

62
00:04:44,718 --> 00:04:46,510
Theta plays the role of t.

63
00:04:47,633 --> 00:04:52,710
So d y d x equals d y d theta over d x d
theta.

64
00:04:53,160 --> 00:05:01,087
d y d theta is r prime sine theta plus r
cosine theta. d x d theta is r prime

65
00:05:01,087 --> 00:05:04,382
cosine theta minus r sine theta.

66
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:12,320
For the cardioid r equals one plus cosine
theta at theta equals pi over two: r is

67
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:15,014
one and r prime is negative one.

68
00:05:15,464 --> 00:05:21,992
d y d theta is negative one, d x d theta
is negative one, so the slope is one.

69
00:05:23,133 --> 00:05:30,024
Horizontal tangents: d y d theta equals
zero. Vertical tangents: d x d theta

70
00:05:30,024 --> 00:05:31,112
equals zero.

71
00:05:31,562 --> 00:05:34,719
Check that the other derivative isn't also
zero.

72
00:05:35,866 --> 00:05:39,429
Don't confuse d r d theta with d y d x.

73
00:05:39,879 --> 00:05:46,645
d r d theta tells whether the curve moves
toward or away from the origin; d y d x is

74
00:05:46,645 --> 00:05:48,498
the slope on the graph.

75
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:55,585
Your turn. For r equals two, what is d y d
x at theta equals pi over four?

76
00:05:56,035 --> 00:05:57,571
Pause the video and try it.

77
00:05:58,021 --> 00:06:04,101
It's a circle. d y d x equals negative
cotangent theta, which is negative one.

78
00:06:05,233 --> 00:06:10,097
In this lesson, a BC topic, we'll find the
area inside polar curves.

79
00:06:11,233 --> 00:06:15,862
In polar, we slice regions into thin
sectors, like pizza slices.

80
00:06:16,312 --> 00:06:22,478
A sector with radius r and angle d theta
has area one half r squared d theta.

81
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:29,466
The area is one half times the integral of
r squared d theta, from alpha to beta.

82
00:06:29,916 --> 00:06:33,052
Make sure the angles trace the region
exactly once.

83
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:39,384
The cardioid r equals one plus cosine
theta, from zero to two pi:

84
00:06:39,834 --> 00:06:45,612
One half times the integral of one plus
two cosine theta plus cosine squared

85
00:06:45,612 --> 00:06:48,196
theta, which is three pi over two.

86
00:06:49,333 --> 00:06:56,024
One petal of r equals cosine two theta
runs from negative pi over four to pi over

87
00:06:56,024 --> 00:06:56,437
four.

88
00:06:56,887 --> 00:07:02,885
Its area is one half times the integral of
cosine squared two theta, which is pi over

89
00:07:02,885 --> 00:07:03,308
eight.

90
00:07:04,433 --> 00:07:10,407
The area between two polar curves is one
half the integral of outer r squared minus

91
00:07:10,407 --> 00:07:11,558
inner r squared.

92
00:07:12,008 --> 00:07:14,120
Find where they intersect to get the
limits.

93
00:07:15,266 --> 00:07:18,445
Your turn. Find the area inside r equals
three.

94
00:07:18,895 --> 00:07:20,431
Pause the video and try it.

95
00:07:20,881 --> 00:07:24,550
One half times nine times two pi, which is
nine pi.

